Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(-kv+hw)=T(-kv)+T(hw)=-kT(v)+hT(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T(-5{v}_{1}+4{v}_{2}) & =-5T({v}_{1})+4T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}23 \\ -24\end{aligned}] & =-5T({v}_{1})+4[\begin{aligned}-3 \\ 4\end{aligned}] \\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =4[\begin{aligned}-3 \\ 4\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}23 \\ -24\end{aligned}] \\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-12 \\ 16\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}23 \\ -24\end{aligned}] \\ 5T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-35 \\ 40\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =\frac{1}{5}[\begin{aligned}-35 \\ 40\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{1}) & =[\begin{aligned}-7 \\ 8\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$
